WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:02.139
Welcome to your initiation.

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:06.500
In a short while, you’ll be a member of
our little family.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.969
But there's something you should know first.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:18.210
In order to be a part of the family, you must
first know the family rules and values.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:23.210
So I'll need you to pay attention to all 43
Things You Missed in Sunny Family Cult.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.580
But first you'll want to have seen the series
over on CryptTV so click or tap right here

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.619
to give that a watch if you haven't seen it
yet.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:33.910
The first requirement of our group is to be
desensitized to violence.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.980
Season 1 is all about moulding Taylor, our
youngest member so far.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.330
Take a look at some of the things we've done
to help her along.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.750
Notice how the house is decorated with diagrams
of human anatomy to get her to see flesh as

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.500
flesh, and nothing more.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:55.500
Even as a young child, she's forced to watch
violent movies.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:01.170
(Clip)

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.950
Not much effort is put into shielding her
from the violent ritual taking place downstairs.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.770
“Come on.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.490
Go to bed.”

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:14.000
Anddd…. that's about all the protection
they give her.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.330
It's almost like they want Taylor to find
out on her own, despite her mother telling

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.890
her she wasn't supposed to see the ritual.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:25.250
And when she does find out, instead of trying
to convince her otherwise, the mom smears

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.250
blood on her daughter's face.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:31.570
They also hint at the idea that Taylor will
be expected to become apart of the cult when

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:32.920
she's older too.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.750
At the very beginning, Taylor is upset that
her parents are leaving and her mom tells

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.060
her she'll go on lots of dates when she's
older too.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.920
Seems harmless enough, but considering their
idea of a date involves chopping up and sacrificing

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.200
a drunk hitchhiker, they're basically planting
the seed that they expect her dates to end

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.810
in bloodshed too, and in episode 3, we see
just that, when Taylor is finally old enough

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.590
to go on dates.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.260
This is where we see Taylor's hesitation starts
to come into play.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.530
A part of her wants to participate in the
cult and make her family proud, but a part

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.030
of her wants to be a normal teenager.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.920
“Do you ever just wish things were different?

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.560
You ever wish you were just somewhere different?

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:17.409
Like you could do whatever you want, and not
have to answer to anyone or follow anyone’s

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:18.409
rules?”

00:02:18.409 --> 00:02:21.920
Season 1 ends with a huge metaphorical choice
on April 1st.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.730
Take note, that April Fools Day is the holiest
day of the year for our family because we

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:33.560
are all about spreading chaos, and that’s
exactly what that day is dedicated to.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.870
Taylor has the option to continue to fight
against her parents ways, or join them and

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.900
let go of ever living a normal life.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:45.859
She chooses her own family in a huge way by
inviting over all of her friends and killing

00:02:45.859 --> 00:02:49.220
them off, thus completing her initiation.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.730
The moment is commemorated with a family photo.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:03:01.889
“I think we should do a family portrait.”

00:03:01.889 --> 00:03:05.950
Photos become a major symbol of Taylor’s
internal struggle between her responsibility

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.480
to the family and her social life.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.969
The family loves to commemorate things with
photos.

00:03:10.969 --> 00:03:15.049
They have like 100 cameras set up in the house
and they have tons of family photos dating

00:03:15.049 --> 00:03:16.760
back to Taylor’s childhood.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.629
In Season 2 she starts to make a real friend
when she grows closer to Jaina, and they take

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:27.159
some Polaroid selfies together, which Taylor
holds very dear in same drawer she keeps her

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:28.159
diary.

00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:31.469
The selfie she took with her family is nowhere
to be seen.

00:03:31.469 --> 00:03:32.930
The lesson to be learned?

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:37.269
Don't stray from the path set for you like
Taylor did.

00:03:37.269 --> 00:03:41.180
One thing you can do to show your dedication
is get a tattoo of our symbol like Taylor

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.629
does when she's sixteen, but if anyone asks,
just say you saw it online and it looked cool,

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:52.159
because we use the same logo on our calling
card, which includes real human blood.

00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:56.299
The logo itself is a smiley face with a line
drawn through the center.

00:03:56.299 --> 00:04:01.089
I’ll get back to the meaning behind that
later in this initiation.

00:04:01.089 --> 00:04:06.430
So that covers Season 1 and Lesson 1, the
development of Taylor from innocent little

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.159
girl to cold blooded killer.

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:13.609
Lesson 2 is going to be about the true purpose
of the cult and a rival cult hinted at in

00:04:13.609 --> 00:04:15.930
both Seasons 1 and 2.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:21.470
But before we get to that, I know you want
to hear about those Easter Eggs, so here they

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:22.470
are.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:27.110
The house is decorated with a lot of repeating
symbols, like these owl statues.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:32.229
They could be a link between owls, a nocturnal
predator, and the family, who makes all of

00:04:32.229 --> 00:04:34.040
their kills at night.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.979
Also, the killer in episode 2 has an owl tattoo.

00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:39.650
More on that later.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:44.319
When Taylor finally snaps and kills 4 classmates,
she you can see the board game Maniac in the

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:45.970
background behind her.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:49.980
And then when her friends tell her, “this
isn't funny” she replies with, “I think

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:54.560
it is,” and a book titled Funny Girl can
be seen behind her.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.380
Then in the classroom, there are some quotes
on the wall.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.060
Many of them are thematic of the entire series.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.070
Like this one.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.069
It's a quote from Woodrow Wilson.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.270
‘The seed of revolution is repression.’

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:10.110
You could apply that to Taylor's struggle
between her father trying to keep her in line

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:13.139
and her trying to revolt and live her own
life.

00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:18.400
Normal teenager stuff, but there's a lot more
on the line when Dad's the leader of a notorious

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.400
cult.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.620
There are other quotes like this about the
series in the classroom, but I'll let you

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.770
check those out for yourself and leave your
findings in the comments.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:31.000
Then there's this S. You maybe remember it
from when you were in school.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.030
I remember the other kids would draw it everywhere.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.030
Constantly.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.060
But I've never actually known the meaning
of it.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.699
So I decided to Google it.

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:42.270
I just literally looked up, ‘the s from
school’, and surprisingly it turned up some

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.270
results…

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.360
however it seems that nobody really knows
the meaning or origin of it.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:51.479
It actually comes up again later in Taylor's
diary along with the words Anti-Social.

00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:55.379
So maybe it's something she draws to pass
the time because she has no friends, or maybe

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:58.630
she even does it to try to fit in more with
the other students.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:02.599
The last find from the classroom I'll point
out is that if you look at the papers on Taylor’s

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:06.310
desk right here, it's actually the shot list
from this scene.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:09.410
Sunny Family loves references to other horror
films.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.370
Taylor has a Nosferatu poster, a reference
to one of the most iconic horror films of

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.949
the 1920s.

00:06:16.949 --> 00:06:20.439
(Clip)

00:06:20.439 --> 00:06:24.449
Then inside of the coffee shop, there's a
figurine on the counter of Giggles the Clown,

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:29.189
another CryptTV property, and Taylor also
has a photo of Giggles in her room.

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:30.189
Remember Look-See?

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:34.009
He's another CryptTV monster that I did a
Things You Missed on a couple weeks ago, and

00:06:34.009 --> 00:06:36.889
a sketch of him can be found in Taylor's diary.

00:06:36.889 --> 00:06:41.220
There's also a drawing of Mordeo, from the
Crypt short film, and her bookmark is connected

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:43.409
to a small metallic knife.

00:06:43.409 --> 00:06:45.850
And whatever this thing is.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:49.860
Now if you've been paying attention so far
to this point, there is probably one thing

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.840
you're a little confused about.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.780
That is, what's the point of the Sunny Family
Cult?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:59.810
In the ritual, the cult leader says the goal
is to introduce chaos and disrupt bonality,

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:03.900
or in other words, spice up the boring everyday
routine of life.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.599
But in private, to Taylor, her parents preach
the value of stopping bad people and not being

00:07:08.599 --> 00:07:09.990
a victim.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.350
So which is it?

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:16.460
The reason for the duality in values is actually
because the cult itself is split.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:17.689
Into two.

00:07:17.689 --> 00:07:23.599
The last thing we see in Season 2 is a flashback
to Elias’s past, when he was first introduced

00:07:23.599 --> 00:07:29.060
into the cult. by this guy, Roger, the guy
who doesn’t look old enough to be a teacher

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.569
because he’s lying.

00:07:30.569 --> 00:07:31.569
“Hey!”

00:07:31.569 --> 00:07:32.569
“Hi.”

00:07:32.569 --> 00:07:36.110
“I don’t mean to bother you or anything.”

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:37.210
He’s lying.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.430
“Are you stalking me?”

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.430
“What?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.430
No.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:42.430
Not at all.”

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:43.849
He’s lying again.

00:07:43.849 --> 00:07:47.749
“The school offered me a full time teaching
gig for next semester.”

00:07:47.749 --> 00:07:48.749
Lying!

00:07:48.749 --> 00:07:52.900
You can probably guess he’s not a detective
either, he was an member of the cult back

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:53.900
in the 90s.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.710
And he still dons the mask and the axe in
present day.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:02.280
He had a disagreement with Elias in 1995 about
their differing ways of thinking.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.280
“I’m sorry.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.381
I can’t do it.

00:08:04.381 --> 00:08:05.800
It doesn’t feel right.”

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:08.900
“You won’t know how it feels until you
do it.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.320
Trust me Elias.”

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.340
“We’re different Roger.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.419
I don’t always have to think the same way
you do.”

00:08:15.419 --> 00:08:16.699
“We’re family.

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:18.509
Maybe you should start trying a little harder.”

00:08:18.509 --> 00:08:23.169
We don’t know exactly what they disagreed
on, but what if this split resulted in two

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:27.699
chapters of the cult, one led by Elias, and
the other by Roger?

00:08:27.699 --> 00:08:33.820
What if that’s why Elias’s cult is dedicated
to stopping to bad people and avoiding victimization,

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:38.260
while still sharing the motto about chaos
and disrupting bonality carried over from

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:40.660
the original cult it branched off from?

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.750
That could explain why members of Elias’s
cult are so different from meeting to meeting,

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.380
because he’s always getting rid of people
who don’t see eye to eye with him.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:54.010
That would mean the copycat in episode 2 might
not be a copycat at all, but rather a member

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.660
of the original chapter of the cult.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.870
Maybe Elias’s group are the real copycats
here.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.150
--
But what was this big disagreement that caused

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:03.620
the cult to split?

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:06.160
Our only clues are in each of the victims.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.530
Let’s break them down one by own.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.980
The first victim is just a drunk hitchhiker.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:15.600
You could argue that he’s guilty for public
intoxication, but this guy probably won’t

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.800
give us any other clues about what caused
the split.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:23.700
Episode 2, however, shows the family taking
out the copycat cult member, who, again, could

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.890
be from the original cult.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:29.460
They tell this guy that he’s being taken
out for going after children, and there’s

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:33.850
one shot in particular that seems to suggest
he might also be taking part in some cannibal

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.780
activities, though it’s never said for sure.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.330
These two ideals may have contributed to the
breakup, but it’s also pretty clear that

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:44.970
the victim during the big disagreement in
the 90s is not a kid, so there are most likely

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.010
other points they disagree on as well.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:51.570
The victim in episode three doesn’t appear
to be doing anything wrong, however pay attention

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:52.570
to this line.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:55.930
“I wish I could like teleport or something.

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:59.160
Ooh, or not live in a dorm.”

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.720
So this guy is in college.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:04.690
It’s later revealed that Taylor is only
16 at this point because her next birthday

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:07.100
in the series is her seventeenth birthday.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.640
Most likely, this guy is on the hit-list because
of that.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:14.350
We don’t know what any of the four classmates
killed in episode 4 did, if anything, but

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:18.590
it certainly brings what the mom said about
killing bad pe-ople into question.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.930
In season 2, Taylor meets her best friend
Jaina, and shortly after, Jaina’s boyfriend

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:27.850
Lance is murdered by what we can almost confirm
is Roger, or at the very least, someone from

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.600
Roger’s chapter of the cult.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:34.140
Not long after, an arm is found in the woods,
and shortly after that a seemingly matching

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.600
body is spotted by Taylor’s classmate Allie-Ann.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:41.800
I think the assumption is that it belongs
to Lance, however, upon closer inspection,

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:46.450
the arm is wearing long red sleeves that Lance
didn’t have at the time of his death.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:51.970
But then, upon closer closer inspection, Lance
does have a red jacket in hand just before

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:56.150
he’s killed, so maybe the killer put the
jacket on him before dismembering the arm

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.610
and dumping the body?

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.610
I’m not sure why though.

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:03.690
The guy who is killed for deserting the family
makes sense for both chapters of the cult,

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:07.890
they can’t have formers members walking
around who could possibly talk.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:11.330
But the death of the high powered attorney
described to Allie-Ann and her friends by

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:15.170
the barista from the coffee shop offers up
some more insight.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:19.270
Supposedly she was crooked, so she got stabbed
to death by The Sunny Family Cult and dumped

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:20.270
in a lake.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:23.800
We don’t know how long ago that was, only
that the barista says he hadn’t seen the

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.490
symbol in a long time.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.810
He does look to be on the younger side, so
there’s a good chance this was after the

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:29.810
split.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:31.640
So what can we conclude from all of this?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:38.290
I would theorize that in 1995 Elias and Roger
disagreed on what qualifies as a bad person.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:41.360
Elias broke off from the group and formed
his own chapter of the cult.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:46.510
The two continued to operate independently
until 2017, when someone from Roger’s group

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:49.680
chopped up… and possibly devoured… a young
girl.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:53.670
After much debate, and even a little push
from his own daughter, Elias decided enough

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:57.580
was enough and went after the guy who had
abducted the young girl.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:02.700
Now, for revenge, Roger comes after Elias’s
family, killing their friends and sparing

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:07.790
their enemies and in the end, kidnapping Taylor,
the girl they’ve been grooming to one day

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.250
be the new leader of the family cult.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.220
I think it’s a sound theory, but it does
leave one question.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:15.960
Who is Jaina?

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:20.370
If you rewatch season 2, she really goes out
of her way to befriend Taylor.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:24.200
She also talks to Roger at the coffee shop,
but we don’t get to see the contents of

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.690
that conversation.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:30.100
But the last time Taylor speaks to her in
Season 2, Jaina says there’s more she info

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.350
hasn’t told yet.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.250
So what is Jaina hiding?

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:37.170
There’s a minor line by Taylor’s mother
in episode 4 where she mentions that they’ll

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.440
need to get more bleach to clean up the bloody
mess.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:43.660
Well, in Season 2, Jaina has bleach stains
on her shirt.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:49.390
Is this the latest fashion trend, or has Jaina
been doing some “cleaning” of her own.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.770
Let me know your thoughts in the comments.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:56.510
But before we’re ready to officially accept
you into our family, before the initiation

00:12:56.510 --> 00:13:01.390
is complete there’s one more thing I’ll
need you to do and that’s to subscribe to

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:06.630
CryptTV, they’ve got new horror content
every week on Tuesdays, Thursdays and Fridays

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:09.550
and they’re getting really close to 1 million
subs.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.390
So let’s go make that happen.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.640
Go ahead and like this video.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.890
And if you haven’t seen it yet, check out
my video 58 Things You Missed in Look-See,

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:20.200
it’s another Crypt series I’ve covered,
so if you enjoy Sunny Family, you’ll want

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.680
to check that one out too.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:26.050
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:29.510
notifications and I’ll you in the next one.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.670
Assuming we both survive.

